#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:16
msgid "1.1 Configuring Blynk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:18
msgid "In this chapter we create a Blynk account, one template and one device, and copy the three lines that go at the top of every project sketch. This is done **once** - all the projects in this kit reuse the same template and the same device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:24
msgid "The Blynk.Console interface is updated from time to time. The screenshots below were taken in 2026. If a button has moved, look for the **field name** (such as ``AUTH TOKEN``) instead of the exact button position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:29
msgid "1. Create an account"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:31
msgid "Go to `BLYNK <https://blynk.io/>`_ and click **Sign Up** in the upper right corner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:36
msgid "Enter your email address, tick the agreement box and click **Sign Up**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:41
msgid "A message asks you to check your inbox. Open the activation link in your mailbox, then create a password."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:48
msgid "2. Create a template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:50
msgid "A **template** is the blueprint: it defines which data the project sends and what the dashboard looks like. Create it once, and add data to it as you work through the projects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:54
msgid "In the left sidebar open **Developer Zone**, then **My Templates**, and click **+ New Template**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:60
msgid "Now set up the template."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:65
msgid "Fill in the form:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:67
msgid "**NAME**: ``Ultimate Sensor Kit``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:68
msgid "**HARDWARE**: **ESP32**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:69
msgid "**CONNECTION TYPE**: **WiFi**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:74
msgid "Click **Done** / **Save** to keep the template."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:79
msgid "At this point the template is **empty** - no datastreams, no events, no dashboard. That is intended: they are added in each project, when you know which data the project needs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:83
msgid "Because every project reuses this one template, each project gets **its own virtual pins**, so the projects never overwrite each other:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:90
msgid "Project"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:91
msgid "Virtual pins"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:92
msgid "Used for"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:93
msgid "Flame Alert System"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:94
msgid "V0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:95
msgid "flame sensor value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:96
msgid "Intrusion Alert System"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:97
msgid "V1 - V2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:98
msgid "away mode, status text"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:99
msgid "Plant Monitor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:100
msgid "V3 - V6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:101
msgid "temperature, humidity, soil, LED"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:102
msgid "Remote Relay Controller"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:103
msgid "V7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:104
msgid "relay state"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:105
msgid "Auto Watering System"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:106
msgid "V8 - V10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:107
msgid "moisture, threshold, auto mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:109
msgid "You do not have to remember the numbers - every project page repeats the pins it uses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:113
msgid "Every datastream has **two names**, and Blynk uses them for different things:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:115
msgid "**DATASTREAM NAME** - the technical name, for example ``away_mode``. This is what the API and MQTT see, and it is written in lower case with underscores."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:117
msgid "**DISPLAY NAME** - what the widgets and dashboards show, for example ``Away Mode``. Blynk fills it in for you by capitalising each word and replacing the underscores with spaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:121
msgid "That is why a widget ends up reading ``Away Mode (V1)`` even though the datastream is called ``away_mode``. The project pages below name the widget by its display name, because that is the text you will actually see on screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:126
msgid "3. Create a device"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:128
msgid "A template on its own has **no** auth token - a device has. The device is the actual board, and it inherits the template."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:131
msgid "In the left sidebar click **Devices**, then **+ New Device**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:136
msgid "Choose **From template**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:141
msgid "Select the template **Ultimate Sensor Kit**, give the device a name, and click **Create**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:147
msgid "A **New Device Created!** window pops up with the three lines you need."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:152
msgid "Copy them **exactly** - one wrong character and the board never connects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:162
msgid "If you close that window, the same information is available again in **Devices** -> your device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:164
msgid "The token belongs to the **device**, not to the template. Adding datastreams to the template later does not change the token, so the sketches keep working."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/00-blynk_config.rst:167
msgid "The template and the device are ready. The next chapter installs the two libraries the sketches need."
msgstr ""
